            p('"Correlation noted," Mission AI added. "The salvage accords\' critics argue that true material sovereignty isn\'t just about technical capability — it\'s about psychological sovereignty, the confidence to see value in what others discard. They contend that a colony that can reclaim materials but still views them as inferior to Earth-imports is not truly exercising material agency."'),
            p('Jonah tapped his console, pulling up the current fabrication statistics. The numbers told a story of transformation: Martian-native alloys now outperformed Earth-sourced equivalents in three critical categories — radiation resistance, thermal cycling durability, and tensile strength under low-gravity conditions. The salvage economy wasn\'t just keeping pace; it was innovating.'),
