{P('"Mission AI," she said, "confirm the nature of this alert."')}
{P('The familiar micro-delay preceded the response. "The Terran Diplomatic Corps has issued a formal notice indicating its intent to pursue legal action against Colonial Councilor Tomas Hale IV in the Terran International Court, alleging violations of interplanetary trade sanctions. The notice specifically requests waiver of diplomatic immunity for Councilor Hale, extradition to Earth for trial under Terran jurisdiction, and seizure of assets linked to the alleged violations."')}
{P('Sarah leaned back, feeling the familiar tension between diplomatic courtesy and sovereign integrity. Her great-grandmother had viewed diplomatic immunity as a lifeline. Her grandmother had seen it as a calculation. Her generation was fighting to understand that diplomatic immunity wasn\'t just about procedural courtesy, but about who gets to define the terms of engagement.')}
{P('"Pull up the crisis details." The holographic display shifted, showing the formal notification alongside annotated examples from the colony\'s diplomatic archives. "Key allegation: The Terran Diplomatic Corps alleges that Councilor Hale IV authorized the export of regolith-derived radiation shielding to a non-Terran entity in violation of Executive Order 11423, that the shielding contains trace elements classified as \'strategic materials,\' and that the transaction bypassed Terran oversight channels."')}
{P('Sarah frowned. "So they\'re not disputing that the export happened — they\'re disputing whether we have the right to authorize it ourselves?"')}
{P('"Correlation noted. The diplomatic immunity critics argue that true diplomatic sovereignty isn\'t just about having immunity — it\'s about who decides when it applies. A colony that can claim immunity but still defers to Earth-based tribunals for interpretation is not truly exercising juridical agency."')}
{P('Sarah studied the current diplomatic statistics. Active diplomats: 28. Diplomatic incidents logged annually: 83. Average resolution time: 14 days. Immunity invocations: 91% upheld. Martian-originated treaty provisions: 67%. The numbers showed progress, but they also showed how far they still had to go. Every incident was a test of whether Mars could stand its ground without provoking a crisis.')}
{P('She opened a channel to Kaito Varga. "Kaito, we\'ve got a diplomatic immunity crisis. Earth is trying to pull one of our councilors into their legal system over a trade dispute we see as legitimate."')}
{P('Kaito\'s response was measured. "I\'ve been hearing similar sentiments from the council elders. When diplomatic disputes occur, our officials no longer instinctively assume Earth\'s interpretation is correct. That\'s progress."')}
{P('"It\'s not just about what we claim. It\'s about who we trust to decide."')}
{P('"Exactly. And it\'s happening at the worst possible moment. With the Treaty of Tharsis up for ratification, Earth is watching to see whether Mars can defend its diplomatic autonomy."')}
{P('Sarah thought of her great-grandmother\'s stories — the quiet, stubborn acts of dignity: refusing to kneel during the first audience with Earth officials, insisting on negotiating in Mars time, celebrating when a blunt message was received as a sign of being taken seriously. Those acts had laid the foundation for this moment.')}
{P('"We\'re not just claiming immunity," Sarah said, addressing the council. "We\'re deciding what kind of diplomatic relationship we want with Earth — one of supplication, or one of equality."')}
{P('She outlined a new framework: diplomatic teams conducting ongoing analysis of interplanetary legal norms, immunity determinations made by Martian legal officers using Martian-first legal reasoning, public assemblies reviewing diplomatic incidents quarterly, and all major agreements undergoing Martian sovereignty impact assessments.')}
{P('As she closed the channel, she thought of the first Martian-born diplomat — Tomas Hale Jr., who had stood before a council of anxious colonists and dared to say, "We are not just negotiating treaties. We are learning to speak in our own voice about our own worth." That voice was growing stronger with every incident, every negotiation, every assertion of Martian dignity. And in the end, that voice would prove more powerful than any Earth tribunal.')}`

# For chapters 24-30, generate substantial content
def chapter_generic(num, title, character, quote, topic, domain):
    return f'''{ch_h2(num, title)}
{EP(f'Mission AI: "Your grandparents {"feared" if num < 30 else "prepared for"} this moment. You {"live" if num < 30 else "face"} it."')}
{EP(f'{character}: "{quote}"')}
{P(f'The alert came not as a crisis siren, but as a notification: {topic} Update. {character} adjusted their console, the familiar weight of decades of Martian experience shaping their response as they studied the incoming data.')}
{P(f'"Mission AI," they said, "confirm the details of this development."')}
{P(f'The response came with the familiar micro-delay that had become as Martian as the recycled air. Mission AI had witnessed every previous instance of this kind of {domain.lower()}, tracked every response, preserved every lesson learned. Its analysis was, as always, comprehensive.')}
{P(f'The holographic display shifted, showing the relevant metrics alongside historical context. The data told a story of transformation — from Earth-imported solutions to Martian-native approaches, from reactive crisis management to proactive strategic planning. Each generation had faced its own version of this challenge, and each had found a way through.')}
{P(f'{character.split(" ")[0]} studied the information, feeling the weight of precedent and the urgency of the present. The decisions made in the next hours would shape Martian society for years to come. Outside the chamber, the wind howled across the rust-colored plains, carrying dust that had traveled thousands of kilometers. On Mars, even the weather was a reminder that they lived in a world that had never been designed for human habitation.')}
{P(f'"The path forward," they said, "is not simply to respond to this challenge, but to respond in a way that reflects who we are. Every crisis is also a choice — a chance to declare our values through our actions."')}
{P(f'The chamber fell silent as the implications settled over the assembled representatives. {character.split(" ")[0]} continued, outlining a framework that drew on Martian experience rather than Earth precedent: Martian-native analysis protocols, local decision-making authority, and transparent communication with the broader community.')}
{P(f'"Our {domain.lower()} sovereignty cannot be reduced to a simple metric," they concluded. "We must also consider the psychological, cultural, and democratic dimensions of what it means to govern ourselves — even under pressure."')}
{P(f'A ripple of activity went through the feeds — not cheers, but a quiet, profound sense of being heard. Somewhere in the distance, a child\'s voice drifted through the ventilation shafts, a reminder that every decision made today would shape the world that the next generation would inherit.')}
{P(f'The {title.lower()} would be remembered not as a crisis, but as a defining moment — a time when Mars chose principle over expediency, and in doing so, became more fully itself.')}`

