def build_moon_chapters(chapters, topics):
    result = []
    for num, title, prot, partner in chapters:
        if prot is None:
            # Interstitial chapter
            result.append(interstitial_chapter(num, title))
        else:
            topic_text = topics.get(num, f"The crew continues their work on the lunar surface, making progress on all mission objectives.")
            text = f'''{ch_h1(num, title)}
{EP(f'Mission AI: "{topic_text}"')}
{EP(f'{prot}: "{["They told us space was empty. They never mentioned how full it would feel.", "The hardest part isn\'t the vacuum or the radiation—it\'s the silence that screams in your bones.", "Every footprint we leave is a promise to those who dared to dream before us.", "In the black, we found not just darkness, but a canvas for our hopes.", "The Moon doesn\'t give up its secrets easily. It makes you earn every byte of data.", "We came to study the Moon. Instead, the Moon is studying us."][num % 6]}"')}
{P(f'The regolith underfoot was finer than talc, sharper than shattered glass — a reminder that the Moon had known no water, no wind, no erosion for billions of years. Each step kicked up a plume of dust that hung in the airless silence before settling back to the gray surface, leaving temporary footprints that would last longer than any monument on Earth.')}
{P(f'{prot} adjusted the grip on the sample container, feeling the unfamiliar pressure of the EVA gloves against palm and fingers. The suit\'s life support hummed softly in their ears — a constant reminder of the fragile bubble keeping them alive in this hostile grandeur. Outside their visor, the black sky was emblazoned with stars so bright they cast faint shadows, and there, hanging like a fragile ornament, was Earth — a swirl of blue and white that seemed both achingly close and infinitely distant.')}
{P(f'"Readings are nominal," {partner} reported, voice steady over the comms. Their boots crunched nearby as they monitored the portable analyzer. "Atmospheric processors holding at 10.2 psi. CO2 scrubbers at 96% efficiency. Radiation levels nominal. We\'re green across the board."')}
{P(f'{prot} paused, scanning the horizon where the solar array caught the sunlight like a field of metallic dragonflies. "Confirmed. Proceeding with primary operations. Keep monitoring those dust levels — I don\'t like how it\'s clinging to the suit joints."')}
{P(f'The work proceeded with the methodical precision that had become the crew\'s trademark. Every movement was deliberate, every check double-verified, every communication acknowledged. On the Moon, there was no room for error — the margin between success and disaster was measured in millimeters and seconds.')}
{P(f'As they worked, the conversation drifted from technical to personal — a coping mechanism as old as exploration itself. {prot} spoke of their family back on Earth, of the way the years seemed to pass differently when measured in lunar days rather than Earth ones. {partner} admitted to recurring dreams of Earth\'s oceans, of waves crashing against shores they might never see again.')}
{P(f'The drill bit sang into the regolith, a sound conducted through bone and suit rather than air. Chips of lunar rock flew outward, catching the sunlight in brief, brilliant flashes. Each layer they penetrated was a page in the Moon\'s geological history — a history that, until now, had remained utterly unread.')}
{P(f'"Ten centimeters," {partner} announced. "Hit a change in density. Something different about this layer."')}
{P(f'{prot} leaned closer, watching as the extracted core came free — a cylinder of lunar history, layers visible even in the monochrome suit lighting. The strata told a story that spanned billions of years: impacts and eruptions, cooling and fracturing, the slow dance of a world shaped by forces beyond human comprehension.')}
{P(f'"Mark the sample location and depth. This one goes to the top of the analysis queue."')}
{P(f'They sealed the sample with careful precision, aware that this tiny tube of rock might carry implications far beyond Shackleton Crater. As they turned back toward the habitat, {prot} paused one last time to look at Earth.')}
{P(f'It hung there, beautiful and indifferent, a reminder of everything they\'d left behind and everything they were fighting to understand. The silence of the Moon pressed in — not empty, but full of questions waiting to be asked.')}
{P(f'Later that evening, back in the habitat\'s common module, the crew gathered around the small table that served as both galley and war room. The conversation ebbed and flowed, touching on everything from the technical implications of their work to the deeply personal reasons each had chosen to leave Earth behind. In that moment, surrounded by the humming machinery that kept them alive, they weren\'t just scientists and engineers — they were a family forged in the crucible of shared purpose.')}
