def interstitial_chapter(num, title, kind):
    paras = [ch_h1(num, title)]
    if kind == "treaty":
        paras += [
            EP('Mission AI: "While the pioneers build their home on the Moon, Earth debates whether to let them keep it."'),
            EP('Ambassador Okonkwo: "The Artemis Accords were supposed to be about cooperation. Now they are about control."'),
            P('On Earth, in the marble halls of Geneva, a very different kind of battle was being fought. The Treaty of Tharsis was supposed to formalize the relationship between Earth and its off-world colonies. Instead, it had become a flashpoint for every unresolved tension between the old world and the new.'),
            P('Ambassador Sarah Okonkwo represented Martian interests in the negotiations. She had been born on Earth but had spent most of her adult life on Mars, and she understood both sides in a way that few could.'),
            P('"The treaty as written," she told the assembly, "gives Earth veto power over Martian resource development, limits Martian technological autonomy, and subjects Martian citizens to Terran courts in all matters involving Earth nationals. This is not a partnership. This is colonialism with a diplomatic veneer."'),
            P('The Earth delegates shifted uncomfortably. They had expected gratitude, not resistance. But Sarah had learned on Mars that survival depended on clear vision and firm boundaries.'),
            P('As the debate continued through days and then weeks, the fate of interplanetary relations hung in the balance. And on the Moon, the pioneers continued their work, unaware that the political future of their entire endeavor was being decided by people who had never worn a spacesuit.'),
            P('In the lunar habitat\'s common room that evening, the crew gathered around the communication terminal, watching the diplomatic feeds. "They are deciding our future up there," one of them said, "and they have never even been off the planet."'),
            P('"That is why we have to succeed," the commander replied. "Not just for ourselves, but to prove that the future belongs to those who are willing to go there and build it."'),
        ]
    elif kind == "independence":
        paras += [
            EP('Mission AI: "While the Moon base grows, Mars prepares to declare itself a nation."'),
            EP('Chancellor Varga: "We did not cross the void to remain subjects."'),
            P('In the Valles Marineris Colonial Council chamber, Kaito Varga addressed the assembled representatives. The atmosphere was electric with the gravity of the moment — not the simulated gravity of the habitat\'s rotating sections, but the weight of history.'),
            P('"Fifty years ago," he began, "our grandparents landed on this world with nothing but hope and the contents of three cargo ships. They survived the first winter by sharing rations, by working shifts that lasted sixteen hours, by refusing to let the cold and the dark break their spirits. They did not ask Earth for permission to survive. They simply survived."'),
            P('He paused. "Now it is our turn. We do not ask Earth for permission to govern ourselves. We simply govern."'),
            P('The debate that followed was fierce, but the outcome was never in doubt. The Martian Declaration of Self-Governance passed with overwhelming support.'),
            P('On the Moon, the base received the news with a mixture of pride and concern. Their fates were now linked to Mars in ways the Artemis Accords had never anticipated. The base commander called a meeting. "This changes our strategic position. We need to decide where our loyalties lie."'),
            P('The discussion that followed was the most difficult the crew had faced since their arrival. Each member brought their own perspective, shaped by their nation of origin, their personal history, and their vision for humanity\'s future. There was no easy answer. But the very act of having the discussion — openly, honestly, with respect for differing views — was itself a declaration of what kind of community they were building.'),
        ]
    elif kind == "declaration":
        paras += [
            EP('Mission AI: "A declaration is words on paper. What comes after is written in blood and oxygen."'),
            EP('Chancellor Varga: "Now we find out who our friends are."'),
            P('The response from Earth was not immediate. For three days, the quantum channels carried nothing but silence — a silence that felt more threatening than any ultimatum. On the fourth day, the transmission arrived, and it was exactly what the Martian council had feared.'),
            P('Earth did not recognize the Declaration of Self-Governance. The Terran Diplomatic Corps issued a formal statement declaring the Martian action null and void under international law and warning that consequences would follow.'),
            P('On the Moon, the base commander called an emergency meeting. "This changes things. If Earth imposes sanctions on Mars, our supply chain will be affected. We need to accelerate our self-sufficiency timeline."'),
            P('The chief engineer spoke up. "We have been running projections on full self-sufficiency. With the current rate of ISRU development, we can achieve 90% closure within eighteen months."'),
            P('"Then we had better start making those breakthroughs," the commander replied. The determination in her voice echoed through the habitat, carrying the same resolve that had driven every generation of pioneers since the first humans had left Earth\'s cradle. They had come to the Moon to explore. Now they would stay to survive. And in the process, they would build something that neither Earth nor Mars could take away.'),
        ]
    elif kind == "blockade":
        paras += [
            EP('Mission AI: "The blockades of Mars are not just about ships and cargo. They are about who controls the future."'),
            EP('General Hale: "We prepared for this. We hoped we would never need those preparations."'),
            P('The Martian blockade began not with a dramatic confrontation, but with a slow strangulation. Earth ships stopped arriving at scheduled intervals. Cargo manifests showed fewer critical items. The supply chain that had sustained Mars for fifty years was being systematically dismantled.'),
            P('In the Valles Marineris Logistics Authority, Director Chen Navarro studied the dwindling inventory numbers. "At current consumption rates, we have fourteen days of high-precision manufacturing components, twenty-two days of specialized pharmaceuticals, and eighteen days of advanced semiconductor substrates."'),
            P('The council chamber fell silent. Everyone knew that Martian production had increased dramatically, but no one had anticipated being cut off completely. The blockade was testing not just their supply chains, but their faith in their own capabilities.'),
            P('On the Moon, the base received the news with concern. The base commander called for an emergency review of all critical systems, accelerating efforts to achieve full self-sufficiency before the supply chain collapsed entirely.'),
        ]
    elif kind == "diplomatic":
        paras += [
            EP('Mission AI: "When the guns fall silent, the arguments begin."'),
            EP('Ambassador Okonkwo: "We will not win this through force of arms. We will win it through force of argument."'),
            P('While the blockade tightened around Mars, a different kind of battle was being fought in the diplomatic corridors of Earth\'s capitals. Ambassador Sarah Okonkwo traveled from Geneva to Washington to Beijing, presenting the Martian case.'),
            P('"We are not asking for special treatment," she told the United Nations General Assembly. "We are asking for what every people in history has earned through their labor and sacrifice: the right to govern themselves."'),
            P('Some listened. Some walked out. But Sarah knew that even the act of speaking was a form of resistance. The story of Mars was being told, and once told, it could not be untold.'),
            P('On the Moon, the crew followed the diplomatic developments with intense interest. From their vantage point in lunar orbit, the arguments of Earth\'s diplomats seemed both urgent and strangely irrelevant. While politicians debated sovereignty and jurisdiction, the pioneers were actually building the future.'),
        ]
    elif kind == "view":
        paras += [
            EP('Mission AI: "The Moon is not just a destination. It is a vantage point from which to see the whole system."'),
            EP('Commander Vargas: "From up here, the boundaries between nations disappear. We are all just Earth, trying to reach beyond itself."'),
            P('From the observation dome of the lunar base, the solar system spread out like a map. Earth hung blue and white in the blackness, its continents tracing familiar patterns. Mars was a red spark, barely visible against the starfield.'),
            P('Elena Vargas stood at the viewport, watching the Earth rise over the lunar horizon for the thousandth time. Each time, the sight struck her anew — the fragility of that blue marble, the thin layer of atmosphere containing all of human history, the vast silence surrounding everything.'),
            P('"They are fighting over who gets to own the future," she said quietly to Rajiv, who had joined her. "But the future does not belong to anyone. It belongs to whoever shows up and builds it."'),
            P('Rajiv nodded. "And we have shown up. We are building. That is all we can do — keep building, keep learning, keep proving that what we are doing here matters."'),
            P('They stood together in the silence of the Moon, watching the Earth turn. The political drama unfolding below felt both immediate and distant — urgent in its implications, yet dwarfed by the vastness of the cosmos. They were building not just a base, but a bridge between worlds, between generations, between what humanity had been and what it was becoming.'),
        ]
    return '\n'.join(paras)

